# Registry pull secret: PLACEHOLDER — human action required

No Secret, ciphertext or credential is generated. This document is not a manifest
and is not a Kustomization resource. The Deployment references forgejo-registry.
Before activation, seal a read:package credential as a strictly name/namespace
bound SealedSecret named forgejo-registry of type kubernetes.io/dockerconfigjson,
separately for {{tenant}}-dev and {{tenant}}-prod. Use the controller public
certificate and stdin-only plaintext; never put plaintext in files, argv or logs.

The authorized onboarding change adds each sealed manifest to its overlay and
its Kustomization together with the consuming deployment. Never add a reference
to a missing file, reuse ciphertext between namespaces, or deploy UNRELEASED.
Live activation must prove a fresh pod pulls successfully; sealing and key escrow remain
human/platform-owned. See golden-path ADR-0014 and the runbook stage onboarding/rotation.
